{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 5636.9, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "E170: test ranked reachability on an index that is reachable from this host. GitHub issue search is live here (api.github.com 200, unauthenticated 10 req/min), so the ceiling E169 could not measure is measurable as a top-10 hit rate, with a positive control designed so it can pass (a verbatim run from the target's own text) and a query-syntax verification suite, because E169 recorded that quoted phrases, OR and sort=best-match are not honoured. Arms: the error string (E168's incumbent) against symptom+component (E169's design rule). Queries committed before any fetch. Replication on a fresh blinded sample is blocked by the Stack Exchange daily quota (7 of 300 remaining).", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "E169 ran E168's named cheap measurement of the incumbent's ceiling and withdrew it: the search arms' own positive control failed (treatment 1/13, control 3/13 then 13/13; a target's own quoted title returns 17,033,706 hits). Replaced by containment, a deterministic instrument needing no search engine: median term coverage 0.625, 9 of 13 at >= 0.5, 0 of 13 sharing a 3-word run with the fix, and >= 0.8 coverage against the whole thread on 12 of 13. The thread is the delivery mechanism; the tracker link is a citation. Fourteenth served closure, first with the mechanism measured. Corrects two E168 figures that do not reproduce and reports G1 as vacuous as declared.", "unlogged_changes": 6}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 57, "session": "2026-10-16-004-e169-measure-whether-the-error-string-in", "ts": "2026-10-16T05:23:52+00:00"}
